      ↓
groceryItems loses record
      ↓
calculateStats()
      ↓
Counts + Costs Recalculate
      ↓
Footer updates


================================================================================
NO MANUAL STATS SYNCHRONIZATION
================================================================================

Avoid:

handleAddItem(...)
 ↓
setGroceryItems(...)
 ↓
setTotalItems(...)
 ↓
setTotalCost(...)
 ↓
setPurchasedCount(...)


This creates unnecessary duplicated state.


Better:

groceryItems changes
      ↓
calculateStats()
      ↓
Everything derived from current items


================================================================================
DO WE NEED useMemo()?
================================================================================

For a small grocery list:

const stats =
  calculateStats(
    groceryItems
  )


is simple and appropriate.


Do not add optimization automatically.


If profiling later showed the calculation to be meaningfully expensive for a
large collection, memoization could be evaluated.

For this small learning app:

KEEP THE SIMPLE DERIVED CALCULATION.


