================================================================================
UNIT TESTING calculateStats()
================================================================================

Because calculateStats() is a pure function, it is easy to test independently.


Example:

import {
  describe,
  expect,
  test
} from 'vitest'

import {
  calculateStats
} from './statsCalculator'


describe(
  'calculateStats',

  () => {

    test(
      'calculates grocery statistics',

      () => {

        const items = [

          {
            id:
              'milk',

            quantity:
              2,

            price:
              3.99,

            purchased:
              true
          },


          {
            id:
              'bread',

            quantity:
              1,

            price:
              2.50,

            purchased:
              false
          }

        ]


        const stats =
          calculateStats(
            items
          )


        expect(
          stats.totalItems
        ).toBe(2)


        expect(
          stats.purchasedItems
        ).toBe(1)


        expect(
          stats.remainingItems
        ).toBe(1)


        expect(
          stats.totalCost
        ).toBeCloseTo(
          10.48
        )


        expect(
          stats.purchasedCost
        ).toBeCloseTo(
          7.98
        )


        expect(
          stats.remainingCost
        ).toBeCloseTo(
          2.50
        )


        expect(
          stats.percentageComplete
        ).toBe(50)

      }
    )


    test(
      'handles an empty list',

      () => {

        const stats =
          calculateStats([])


        expect(
          stats.totalItems
        ).toBe(0)


        expect(
          stats.totalCost
        ).toBe(0)


        expect(
          stats.percentageComplete
        ).toBe(0)


        expect(
          stats.averageLineCost
        ).toBe(0)

      }
    )

  }
)


================================================================================
WHY is calculateStats() EASY TO TEST?
================================================================================

It doesn't depend on:

• DOM

• React rendering

• Browser APIs

• Component state


It is simply:

items
 ↓
calculateStats()
 ↓
stats


That is one benefit of separating calculation logic from presentation.


